From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vladimir Levin <vmpstr@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:40:11 -0700
Subject: Avoid flat tree traversal when unlocking a display lock

DisplayLockContext::SetRequestedState() called ForceLockIfNeeded() on
every state change. ForceLockIfNeeded() walks the flat tree to find out
if a newly requested lock is on the ancestor chain of the node of an
active forced update scope. This is not needed when unlocking.

DisplayLockContext::DetachLayoutTree() requests an unlock, and it can be
called during slot assignment recalc, where flat tree traversal is not
allowed. The traversal could then recalc the slot assignment of another
shadow root while the assigned nodes of the slots being recalculated
were not up to date. As a result, parts of the layout tree were not
detached when they left the flat tree.

Only call ForceLockIfNeeded() when a lock is requested.

Also make ScrollMarkerGroupData::ChooseMarkerRecursively() more robust.
It runs after layout, and its flat tree walks must not recalc slot
assignments. It now ignores scroll markers whose scroll targets are not
connected, runs on a stable list of scroll markers instead of the live
focus group, and verifies that no slot assignment recalc happens.

Bug: 570167919
Change-Id: Ib2912912fabbc4368e6eea0c80ef88b0dfe5a9f9
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8550701
Commit-Queue: Vladimir Levin <vmpstr@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen <futhark@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1717859}

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/display_lock/display_lock_context.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/display_lock/display_lock_context.cc
index 4937b8a62bfb660e6fb9f25d783dc688d4647399..a3bff0f5dcbe430e6d00f080d35ebbd8e274bedf 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/display_lock/display_lock_context.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/display_lock/display_lock_context.cc
@@ -120,9 +120,16 @@ void DisplayLockContext::SetRequestedState(EContentVisibility state) {
   NotifyRenderAffectingStateChanged();
 
   // Since our state changed, check if we need to create a scoped force update
-  // object.
-  element_->GetDocument().GetDisplayLockDocumentState().ForceLockIfNeeded(
-      element_.Get());
+  // object. This is only needed if a lock is requested: there is nothing to
+  // force if we are unlocking. This matters, since DetachLayoutTree() requests
+  // an unlock, and it can be called during slot assignment recalc, where flat
+  // tree traversal (as done by ForceLockIfNeeded()) is not allowed. Such a
+  // traversal could recalc the slot assignment of another shadow root, while
+  // the assigned nodes of the slots being recalculated are not up to date.
+  if (state_ != EContentVisibility::kVisible) {
+    element_->GetDocument().GetDisplayLockDocumentState().ForceLockIfNeeded(
+        element_.Get());
+  }
 }
 
 const ComputedStyle* DisplayLockContext::AdjustElementStyle(
